+# Customer credit control - notes
+
+Nothing could be run here (no shell, no database), so none of this has been executed. Please run the upgrade on a copy first.
+
+## What changed and where
+
+**Schema / rollout (BRD 7, 8)**
+- `sql/updates/44.php` (numbered upgrade, idempotent, uses the helpers so other DB types are not broken): `debtorsmaster.nextreviewdate`, `companies.latechargeact` and `baddebtact`, tables `creditreviews`, `creditreminders`, `creditreminderitems`, `creditcharges`, config rows, systypes 13 (Late Payment Charge) and 14 (Bad Debt Write-off), security token 21 (Credit Control, given to role 8), scripts and the five AR menu items. Existing customers get a first review date one interval from the upgrade.
+- Same content for fresh installs: `install/sql/tables/*.sql` (4 new, `debtorsmaster`, `companies`), `install/sql/data/{config,systypes,securitytokens,securitygroups,scripts,menuitems}.sql`, `install/sql/demo.sql`, `sql/demo.sql`, and the `companies` insert in `includes/InstallFunctions.php`. Demo data uses accounts 8200 (income) and 7900 (bad debt); a plain install leaves both `0` (unset) and the pages refuse to post until they are chosen.
+- Reviews, reminders, charges have foreign keys to `debtorsmaster`. `Customers.php` delete removes them with the customer (in a transaction); `Z_ChangeCustomerCode.php` moves them and carries `nextreviewdate`. I also made the customer delete stop when users or contracts exist (it only warned before and deleted anyway).
+
+**Screens (all on the receivables menus; manual in `doc/Manual/ManualAccountsReceivable.html`, bookmarks CreditReviews, CreditReviewDue, CreditReminders, LateCharges, BadDebtWriteOff)**
+- `CreditReviews.php`: record a review (review row + limit/hold/next date in one transaction), history newest first, void a mistaken review, reminders sent and charges for the customer. A logged-in customer sees only reminders and charges.
+- `CreditReviewDue.php`: overdue/due-soon list with balance, overdue, limit, credit available (`GetCreditAvailable`), last paid; screen or PDF.
+- `CreditReminders.php`: preview, untick to leave out, send PDF letters by email to statement contacts; failures are listed and not recorded.
+- `LateCharges.php`: monthly interest + fee, one charge per customer per month (unique key), type 13.
+- `BadDebtWriteOff.php`: write-off of chosen invoices or whole balance, type 14, allocated to the invoices.
+- `includes/CreditControlFunctions.php`: shared helpers (token check, salesman/customer visibility, ageing SQL, hold gate, review save, posting).
+
+**Hold, permissions, visibility (BRD 2, 6)**
+- Hold state is the existing `holdreasons.dissallowinvoices`: 0 ok, 1 hold, 2 watch (the code already treated 2 as a warning). `CreditStatus.php` can now define a watch status.
+- Hold gate (`CreditInvoicingBlock`) added to `DeliveryDetails.php` (staff orders), `ConfirmDispatch_Invoice.php` (invoicing entered orders), `RecurringSalesOrdersProcess.php`, `EDIProcessOrders.php`, `api/includes/api_salesorders.php` (`InsertSalesOrderHeader`, `InvoiceSalesOrder`). `CounterSales.php` and `SpecialOrder.php` already refused held customers.
+- Hold, limit and next review date can only change through a review by a token-21 user: `Customers.php` (fields read-only, UPDATE no longer writes them), `Z_ImportDebtors.php` (update no longer writes them), `api_customers.php` (`ModifyCustomer` needs token 21 for these fields; `InsertCustomer` for `holdreason`; `nextreviewdate` is validated, error 1901; 1900 = customer on hold, 1902 = credit control only).
+- Salespeople: lists/reports filter on `custbranch.salesman` for customers and `debtortrans.salesperson` for transactions.
+
+**Money (BRD 3-5)**
+- Past due uses exactly the `due` / overdue1 / overdue2 expressions of `CustomerInquiry.php`, `PrintCustStatements.php` and `AgedDebtors.php` (`CreditReminderLevelSQL`): level 1 = "Now Due" bucket, 2 = first overdue band, 3 = second band.
+- Charges and write-offs are `debtortrans` rows in the customer's currency with GL entries in the same period when `gllink_debtors` is on. Write-off exchange difference is posted exactly as `CustomerAllocations.php` does (sales exchange difference account against debtors control). Both accounts must be P&L and not a control account; `GLAccounts.php` refuses to delete them, `Z_ChangeGLAccountCode.php` renames them, `CompanyPreferences.php` edits them, `SystemParameters.php` holds the rate, fee, interval and the three letter texts.
+- `PrintCustTrans.php?InvOrCredit=Charge` prints a charge (emailing goes through the same page).
+
+## Ambiguities and how I resolved them
+- "Past due": the reports show an invoice in "Now Due" from its due date itself, so a reminder level 1 starts then, not the day after.
+- A customer on hold gets the final-notice wording and is recorded as level 3, so it also counts as a final notice for the fee.
+- Same level not twice "for the same invoices": a letter lists all overdue items; it is allowed only if at least one item has not yet been reminded at that level.
+- Interest: annual rate on the invoice's current balance for each day of the chosen month after its due date (days/365); late charges themselves do not attract interest. The fee is in home currency and converted at the current rate. The month must have ended; a charge is dated the month's last day.
+- "Correct one entered by mistake": voiding (kept, struck through, with who/why) rather than deleting, for the auditors. It does not reverse a limit/hold change.
+- "Watch" is also an outcome in the review form, in addition to the five listed.
+- Credit-control token is 21 and goes to the System Administrator role only; create a role for Maria and her deputy and give it token 21 (and the receivables menus, which are seeded for all roles).
+- Charges/write-offs are not offered for print in `CustomerInquiry.php` rows (the row list shows them as miscellaneous transactions); print is via `PrintCustTrans.php`. Customer-login visibility of charges relies on the existing transaction screens plus the new page.
+
+## Not done / to check
+- Not done: `SelectCustomer.php` link (the Credit Reviews link is on the customer inquiry and edit pages), print/email links for type 13 rows in `CustomerInquiry.php`/`CustomerAccount.php`, `Contracts.php` order creation is not gated, the legacy `sql/mysql/upgrade*.sql` files are untouched.
+- Untested: all SQL and PHP; email sending depends on the SMTP/mail setup.
